= Solution
{parent=4}

Under $SU(3)_c\times SU(2)_L\times U(1)_Y$, one generation consists of
$$
Q_L:(\mathbf3,\mathbf2)_{1/6},\quad
u_R:(\mathbf3,\mathbf1)_{2/3},\quad
d_R:(\mathbf3,\mathbf1)_{-1/3},
$$
$$
L_L:(\mathbf1,\mathbf2)_{-1/2},\quad
e_R:(\mathbf1,\mathbf1)_{-1},\quad
\nu_R:(\mathbf1,\mathbf1)_0.
$$
These are the fundamental fermions of the <Standard Model> augmented by a right-handed neutrino.

Solved by gpt-5.6-sol high.

= i
{parent=4}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=i}

A Dirac mass term directly pairs a left-handed weak doublet with a right-handed weak singlet and is therefore not electroweak gauge invariant. Introduce the <Higgs doublet> $H:(\mathbf1,\mathbf2)_{1/2}$ and $\widetilde H=i\sigma_2H^*:(\mathbf1,\mathbf2)_{-1/2}$. The gauge-invariant <Yukawa coupling>[Yukawa terms] are
$$
-\bar Q_LY_dHd_R-\bar Q_LY_u\widetilde Hu_R
-\bar L_LY_eHe_R-\bar L_LY_\nu\widetilde H\nu_R+\text{h.c.}
$$
When <electroweak symmetry breaking> gives $\langle H\rangle=(0,v_H/\sqrt2)^T$, these become Dirac mass matrices $M_f=Y_fv_H/\sqrt2$.

Solved by gpt-5.6-sol high.

= ii
{parent=4}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=ii}

Two complex $N\times N$ quark Yukawa matrices contain $4N^2$ real parameters. Flavour-basis transformations $U(N)_Q\times U(N)_u\times U(N)_d$ remove $3N^2-1$, because the common baryon-number phase remains unbroken. Thus there are
$$
N^2+1=2N+\frac{N(N-1)}2+\frac{(N-1)(N-2)}2
$$
physical parameters: $2N$ quark masses, $N(N-1)/2$ mixing angles, and $(N-1)(N-2)/2$ complex phases. A physical phase exists only for $N\geq3$ and produces <CP violation>, equivalently time-reversal violation when CPT is conserved.

Solved by gpt-5.6-sol high.

= iii
{parent=4}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=iii}

Biunitary diagonalization uses independent left rotations for the up and down Yukawa matrices. Their mismatch is the <Cabibbo-Kobayashi-Maskawa matrix> $V=U_{uL}^\dagger U_{dL}$. For two generations it can be made real and is
$$
V=\begin{pmatrix}\cos\theta_c&\sin\theta_c\\-\sin\theta_c&\cos\theta_c\end{pmatrix}.
$$
In the mass basis,
$$
\mathcal L_{\rm weak}\propto
W_\mu^+\bar u_{Li}\bar\sigma^\mu V_{ij}d_{Lj}
+W_\mu^-\bar d_{Lj}\bar\sigma^\mu V_{ij}^*u_{Li}.
$$
The off-diagonal entries permit charged-current flavour change, for example $W^+\to u\bar s$ or semileptonic kaon decay; both vanish when $\theta_c=0$.

Solved by gpt-5.6-sol high.
